# =============================================================================
#  libasm — .gitignore
#
#  Deliberately KEPT in the repo, because they're the point of publishing it:
#    lessons/        the write-ups
#    assets/*.svg    the diagrams those lessons reference
#    LEARNING_PLAN.md, LESSON_PLAN.md, REGISTER_CHEATSHEET.md
#    srcs/ includes/ tests/ docker/ Makefile
# =============================================================================

# --- build output ------------------------------------------------------------
# nasm objects, the archives, and nasm's -MD dependency files.
*.o
*.a
*.d
obj/
tests/.objs/

# Binaries. Git can't spot an extensionless executable on its own, so they have
# to be named. Add yours here if you build under a different name.
libasm_tests
test_libasm
practice
a.out
*.out

# --- debugger / profiler leftovers -------------------------------------------
core
core.*
vgcore.*
.gdb_history
*.dSYM/
callgrind.out.*
massif.out.*
perf.data*

# --- local tooling, not other people's business ------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# --- editor / OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
._*
.AppleDouble
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db

# --- scratch -----------------------------------------------------------------
# practice.s is where you experiment with _start; the Makefile already skips it
# when assembling. Uncomment if you'd rather not publish your scratchpad.
# practice.s
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.log
.env
*.local

# --- the 42 subject ----------------------------------------------------------
# 42's PDF, not yours to redistribute — and 1.3 MB of binary in a repo whose
# value is the text you wrote. Delete this line if you disagree.
en.subject.pdf
*.subject.pdf
